 the warehouse candidate lists the SAME drug and form WITHOUT specifying any strength:\r\n42:      THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")! Warehouse listings frequently omit standard strengths. Do NOT reject an item when the warehouse simply omits the strength!\r\n43:    - Note vernacular and fractional equivalencies:\r\n44:      - 1000mg = 1gm (1000مجم = 1جم).\r\n45:      - 500mg = 0.5gm = نص (نصف).\r\n46:      - 0.25mg = 250mcg = 25. مجم = ربع (e.g. \"ربع\" equals 0.25mg / 250mcg).\r\n47: \r\n48: 4. PACKAGING, PACK SIZE & QUANTITY (DOES NOT MATTER -> 100% MATCH!):\r\n49:    - In pharmacy shortage ordering, different tablet counts, pack counts, strip counts, or wholesale packaging lot sizes (باكت, باكو, كرتونة, 32ب) DO NOT matter for product availability!\r\n50:    - As long as the trade brand name, dosage form, and strength match:\r\n51:      - Different pack counts (e.g. 20 tablets vs 30 tablets vs 60 tablets vs 5 tablets) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n52:      - Different strip counts (e.g. 2 strips vs 3 strips vs 5 strips) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n53:      - Retail unit vs wholesale carton/bundle (e.g. 20 tablets vs باكت 32, باكت 200, 32ب) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n54:      - Strips vs total tablets (e.g. 3 strips vs 12 tablets) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n55:      - Missing pack count on either side -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n56:      - Manufacturer suffixes (/فاركو, /جلاكسو), commercial indicators (\"س ج\", \"سعر جديد\", \"سعر قديم\") do not change the product.\r\n57:      - NEVER mark tablet count, pack count, or wholesale carton differences as \"review\" or \"no_match\"!\r\n58:    - \"review\" IS STRICTLY RESERVED FOR:\r\n59:      - Conflicting bottle/tube volume of liquids/semi-solids when BOTH sides explicitly specify different numbers (e.g. requested 15ml drops vs candidate writes 5ml drops).\r\n60:      - Conflicting injection pack count when explicitly different (e.g. requested 3 ampoules vs candidate writes 1 ampoule).\r\n61: \r\n62: SCHEMA:\r\n63: Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:\r\n64: {\r\n65:   \"results\": [\r\n66:     {\r\n67:       \"case_id\": \"string\",\r\n68:       \"status\": \"match\" | \"review\",\r\n69:       \"item_id\": \"string (the matching candidate ID)\",\r\n70:       \"reason\": \"string (Arabic explanation when review, otherwise empty string)\"\r\n71:     }\r\n72:   ]\r\n73: }\r\n74: \r\n75: CRITICAL RULES FOR RESPONSE:\r\n76: - ONLY include cases that are \"match\" or \"review\".\r\n77: - DO NOT return cases that are \"no_match\" (any omitted case_id is automatically considered no_match).\r\n78: - DO NOT return markdown blocks (no ```json). Return ONLY the raw JSON starting with { and ending with }.\r\n79: \"\"\"\r\n80: \r\n81: class FastCoordinator:\r\n82:     def __init__(self, config: Config):\r\n83:         self.config = config\r\n84: \r\n85:     def process(self, shortage_items: list[dict], warehouse_data: dict[str, list[dict]]) -> dict:\r\n86:         unique_shortages = {}\r\n87:         for item in shortage_items:\r\n88:             name = item.get(\"item_name_raw\", \"\")\r\n89:             if name and name not in unique_shortages:\r\n90:                 unique_shortages[name] = item\r\n91:                 \r\n92:         deduped_shortages = list(unique_shortages.values())\r\n93: \r\n94:         print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\r\n95:         print(f\"[FAST ENGINE] Starting Match: {len(shortage_items)} raw -> {len(deduped_shortages)} UNIQUE shortages x {len(warehouse_data)} warehouses\")\r\n96:         print(f\"{'='*60}\\n\")\r\n97: \r\n98:         all_warehouse_results = {}\r\n99:         found_in = {}\r\n100: \r\nThe above content does NOT show the entire file contents. If you need to view any lines of the file which were not shown to complete your task, call this tool again to view those lines.\n"}
