s or combination types conflict, YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\n   - If dosage form is not mentioned on one side, assume compatible if brand matches, EXCEPT for Drops (نقط/قطرة) which strictly require drops on both sides.\n\n3. STRENGTH / CONCENTRATION:\n   - MULTI-STRENGTH COMBINATIONS: Strengths with slashes like 4/30, 10/20, 12.5/5 represent multi-active ingredient formulations. A multi-strength (e.g. 4/30) MUST NEVER match a single strength (e.g. 4) -> RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\n   - CONFLICTING NUMERIC STRENGTH (Zero Tolerance): If BOTH sides explicitly specify DIFFERENT, CONFLICTING numeric strengths (e.g. requested 500mg vs candidate explicitly specifies 1000mg or 250mg, or 40mg vs 20mg): YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\n   - MISSING STRENGTH IN WAREHOUSE (Default MATCH): If the requested shortage specifies a strength (e.g. 25mg, 500mg, 40mg), but the warehouse candidate lists the SAME drug and form WITHOUT specifying any strength:\n     THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")! Warehouse listings frequently omit standard strengths. Do NOT reject an item when the warehouse simply omits the strength!\n   - Note vernacular and fractional equivalencies:\n     - 1000mg = 1gm (1000مجم = 1جم).\n     - 500mg = 0.5gm = نص (نصف).\n     - 0.25mg = 250mcg = 25. مجم = ربع (e.g. \"ربع\" equals 0.25mg / 250mcg).\n\n4. PACKAGING, PACK SIZE & QUANTITY (DOES NOT MATTER -> 100% MATCH!):\n   - In pharmacy shortage ordering, different tablet counts, pack counts, strip counts, ampoule counts, or wholesale packaging lot sizes (باكت, باكو, كرتونة, 32ب) DO NOT matter for product availability!\n   - As long as the trade brand name, dosage form, and strength match:\n     - Different ampoule counts (e.g. 3 ampoules vs 6 ampoules vs 1 ampoule vs 25 ampoules / 6امبول vs 3امبول) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\n     - Different pack counts (e.g. 20 tablets vs 30 tablets vs 60 tablets vs 5 tablets) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\n     - Different strip counts (e.g. 2 strips vs 3 strips vs 5 strips) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\n     - Retail unit vs wholesale carton/bundle (e.g. 20 tablets vs باكت 32, باكت 200, 32ب) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\n     - Strips vs total tablets (e.g. 3 strips vs 12 tablets) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\n     - Missing pack count or quantity on either side -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\n     - Manufacturer suffixes (/فاركو, /جلاكسو), commercial indicators (\"س ج\", \"سعر جديد\", \"سعر قديم\") do not change the product.\n     - NEVER mark tablet count, ampoule count, pack count, or wholesale carton differences as \"review\" or \"no_match\"!\n\n5. THE \"REVIEW\" (يحتاج مراجعة) SAFETY NET:\n   - \"review\" is the essential SAFETY NET for the pharmacist to manually inspect borderline cases.\n   - If there is any doubt, borderline OCR scanning, minor ambiguity, or 25%–70% plausibility:\n     ALWAYS ROUTE TO \"review\" instead of rejecting to \"no_match\"!\n   - A potential match in \"review\" allows the pharmacist to verify availability in the warehouse, whereas dropping an item into \"no_match\" causes the pharmacy to lose an available medicine.\n   - Examples for \"review\":\n     - Conflicting bottle/tube volume of liquids/semi-solids when BOTH sides explicitly specify different numbers (e.g. requested 15ml drops vs candidate writes 5ml drops).\n     - Borderline OCR where brand letters are slightly ambiguous but plausibly the same drug.\n     - When you are uncertain between \"review\" and \"no_match\": ALWAYS CHOOSE \"review\".","StartLine":22,"TargetContent":"   - Allow common OCR scanning artifacts, dropped letters/syllables, phonetic variants, and Arabic/Persian letter substitutions of the SAME exact brand (like جرانتريل/جرانتيل, امبوفير/اميفير, ديباكين/ديبيكان, or dropped initial 'ا', dropped single letters or missing dots like 'ن' or 'ب', Persian/Urdu letters like پ for 