isually confused OCR letters like 'ف' vs 'د', or slight vowel variations).\r\n23: \r\n24: 2. DOSAGE FORM & FORMULATION (ZERO TOLERANCE FOR CONFLICTS):\r\n25:    - Dosage forms MUST be strictly compatible:\r\n26:      - Tablets/Capsules (اقراص, كبسول, حبوب, فيلم, شريط) ONLY match Tablets/Capsules.\r\n27:      - Syrups/Suspensions (شراب, شرب, معلق) ONLY match Syrups. NEVER match tablets with syrup.\r\n28:      - Creams (كريم) ONLY match Creams. NEVER match cream with ointment or suppository.\r\n29:      - Ointments (مرهم, دهان) ONLY match Ointments. Ointment and Cream are strictly different forms!\r\n30:      - Injections/Ampoules (امبول, حقن, فيال) ONLY match Injections.\r\n31:      - Suppositories (لبوس) ONLY match Suppositories.\r\n32:      - Drops (نقط, قطرة) ONLY match Drops. NEVER match drops with tablets or plain numbers without drops (e.g. كتافلام نقط does NOT match كتافلام 50).\r\n33:      - Sprays (بخاخ, سبراي) ONLY match Sprays.\r\n34:    - COMBINATION PRODUCTS (Zero Tolerance): Commercial suffixes like \"كو\" (Co), \"كومب\" (Comp), \"بلس\" (Plus) denote a multi-ingredient combination product (e.g. adding a diuretic or second active agent). A combination product (e.g. \"دواء كو\" / \"Drug Co\") MUST NEVER match a single-ingredient plain product (\"دواء\" / \"Drug\"). Return \"no_match\".\r\n35:    - If dosage forms or combination types conflict, YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\r\n36:    - If dosage form is not mentioned on one side, assume compatible if brand matches, EXCEPT for Drops (نقط/قطرة) which strictly require drops on both sides.\r\n37: \r\n38: 3. STRENGTH / CONCENTRATION:\r\n39:    - MULTI-STRENGTH COMBINATIONS: Strengths with slashes like 4/30, 10/20, 12.5/5 represent multi-active ingredient formulations. A multi-strength (e.g. 4/30) MUST NEVER match a single strength (e.g. 4) -> RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\r\n40:    - CONFLICTING NUMERIC STRENGTH (Zero Tolerance): If BOTH sides explicitly specify DIFFERENT, CONFLICTING numeric strengths (e.g. requested 500mg vs candidate explicitly specifies 1000mg or 250mg, or 40mg vs 20mg): YOU MUST RETURN \"status\": \"no_match\".\r\n41:    - MISSING STRENGTH IN WAREHOUSE (Default MATCH): If the requested shortage specifies a strength (e.g. 25mg, 500mg, 40mg), but the warehouse candidate lists the SAME drug and form WITHOUT specifying any strength:\r\n42:      THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")! Warehouse listings frequently omit standard strengths. Do NOT reject an item when the warehouse simply omits the strength!\r\n43:    - Note vernacular and fractional equivalencies:\r\n44:      - 1000mg = 1gm (1000مجم = 1جم).\r\n45:      - 500mg = 0.5gm = نص (نصف).\r\n46:      - 0.25mg = 250mcg = 25. مجم = ربع (e.g. \"ربع\" equals 0.25mg / 250mcg).\r\n47: \r\n48: 4. PACKAGING, PACK SIZE & QUANTITY (DOES NOT MATTER -> 100% MATCH!):\r\n49:    - In pharmacy shortage ordering, different tablet counts, pack counts, strip counts, ampoule counts, or wholesale packaging lot sizes (باكت, باكو, كرتونة, 32ب) DO NOT matter for product availability!\r\n50:    - As long as the trade brand name, dosage form, and strength match:\r\n51:      - Different ampoule counts (e.g. 3 ampoules vs 6 ampoules vs 1 ampoule vs 25 ampoules / 6امبول vs 3امبول) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n52:      - Different pack counts (e.g. 20 tablets vs 30 tablets vs 60 tablets vs 5 tablets) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n53:      - Different strip counts (e.g. 2 strips vs 3 strips vs 5 strips) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n54:      - Retail unit vs wholesale carton/bundle (e.g. 20 tablets vs باكت 32, باكت 200, 32ب) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n55:      - Strips vs total tablets (e.g. 3 strips vs 12 tablets) -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n56:      - Missing pack count or quantity on either side -> THIS IS A 100% MATCH (\"status\": \"match\")!\r\n57:      - Manufacturer suffixes (/فاركو, /جلاكسو), commercial indicators (\"س ج\", \"سعر جديد\", \"سعر قديم\") do not change the product.\r\n58:      - NEVER mark tablet count, ampoule count, pack count, or wholesale carton differences as \"review\" or \"no_match\"!\r\n59: \r\n60: 5. THE \"REVIEW\" (يحتاج مراجعة) SAFETY NET:\r\n61:    - \"review\" is the essential SAFETY NET for the pharmacist to manually inspect borderline cases.\r\n62:    - If there is any doubt, borderline OCR scanning, minor ambiguity, or 25%–70% plausibility:\r\n63:      ALWAYS ROUTE TO \"review\" instead of rejecting to \"no_match\"!\r\n64:    - A potential match in \"review\" allows the pharmacist to verify availability in the warehouse, whereas dropping an item into \"no_match\" causes the pharmacy to lose an available medicine.\r\n65:    - Examples for \"review\":\r\n66:      - Conflicting bottle/tube volume of liquids/semi-solids when BOTH sides explicitly specify different numbers (e.g. requested 15ml drops vs candidate writes 5ml drops).\r\n67:      - Borderline OCR where brand letters are slightly ambiguous but plausibly the same drug.\r\n68:      - When you are uncertain between \"review\" and \"no_match\": ALWAYS CHOOSE \"review\".\r\n69: \r\n70: SCHEMA:\r\n71: Return ONLY a valid JSON object matching this schema:\r\n72: {\r\n73:   \"results\": [\r\n74:     {\r\n75:       \"case_id\": \"string\",\r\n76:       \"status\": \"match\" | \"review\",\r\n77:       \"item_id\": \"string (the matching candidate ID)\",\r\n78:       \"reason\": \"string (Arabic explanation when review, otherwise empty string)\"\r\n79:     }\r\n80:   ]\r\n81: }\r\n82: \r\n83: CRITICAL RULES FOR RESPONSE:\r\n84: - ONLY include cases that are \"match\" or \"review\".\r\n85: - DO NOT return cases that are \"no_match\" (any omitted case_id is automatically considered no_match).\r\n86: - DO NOT return markdown blocks (no ```json). Return ONLY the raw JSON starting with { and ending with }.\r\n87: \"\"\"\r\n88: \r\n89: class FastCoordinator:\r\n90:     def __init